description: When working with Inertia.js forms and UI components that expect form props (like TextInput), always use the `createFormAdapter` utility from `@/utils/form-adapters`.## Standard Usage:```typescript import { createFormAdapter } from '@/utils/form-adapters'; // In your component const { data, setData, errors, clearErrors } = useForm({    // your form fields }); // Create the adapter const formAdapter = createFormAdapter({ data, setData, errors, clearErrors }); // Use with TextInput or other form components <TextInput form={formAdapter} name="fieldName" />``` Special Cases: 1. BaseEntitySheet Components BaseEntitySheet automatically provides `formAdapter` in its render props: ```typescript <BaseEntitySheet> {({ formAdapter }) => ( <TextInput form={formAdapter} name="fieldName" /> )} </BaseEntitySheet> ``` 2. Custom Field Formatting For fields that need special formatting (like CEP, phone numbers, etc.), create a custom adapter ```typescript const customFormAdapter = { data, setData: (key: string, value: string | number | boolean | File | null | undefined) => { if (key === 'special_field') { setData(key, formatValue(value)); } else { setData(key, value); }}, errors, clearErrors };``` DO NOT: - Create manual form objects with inline setData wrappers - Use `handleSetData` or other custom wrapper functions - Pass individual form properties to TextInput. NEVER MODIFY form-adapters.ts.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
